it was a bizarre scene in a region where  controversy on the football pitch is not  uncommon  five minutes after the world cup  qualifier kicked off brazilian health  officials came on to the pitch  total confusion many of the world's best  players including argentina's leo messi  and brazil's neymar had never seen  anything like it the officials said four  argentine players had given false  information about their covid 19 status  three of them were on the pitch at the  time and shortly afterwards the world  cup qualifier was suspended the players  returned to their hotels the few fans  allowed into the sao paulo stadium  drifted home angry and confused  [Music]  the health officials did the right thing  because of the coronavirus problem that  we have in this country and the world is  also facing we cannot hesitate it was  not our fault it's the player's fault  who did not comply with the quarantine  it's an awkward situation the official  should have removed the players before  they arrived at the stadium they  shouldn't have let him be on the team  it's the law but it's very hypocritical  i think there are much things than this  and the authorities do nothing  brazilian coveted 19 regulations state  that anyone entering the country who's  been in the united kingdom in the  preceding 14 days was quarantined for 14  days  four of the argentine squad play in the  english premier league nine brazilian  players in the same league stayed in the  uk  the argentine manager leonol scaloni  said no one had told him anything the  argentine football association said it  had complied with the protocol approved  by all the south american footballing  authorities  the match between these two  long-standing rivals came just two  months after argentina beat brazil in  rio de janeiro to win the regional  copper america tournament  and just two days before brazil  celebrates its independence day when  thousands are expected to march in  support of president jar bolsonaro  he's attracted widespread criticism for  his handling of the pandemic the  coronavirus has killed 583 000  brazilians and infected 21 million one  of the worst records in the world  however the football amid widespread  criticism had continued  until now  daniel schweiner al jazeera buenos aires
 

